course: dictionary
lesson: 12468
title: Deflect: turning things away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To deflect something means to make it change direction, often by hitting it. A ball that bounces off a player has been deflected. «The defender's knee deflected the shot into the net.» The shot hit the knee and went somewhere new, so deflected means changed direction.
explain: You can also deflect a question, attention or blame. This means you turn it away from yourself or onto someone else. «When Sam broke the vase, he tried to deflect the blame onto his little brother.» Sam did not want the blame, so he sent it somewhere else.
explain: Scientists use the word too. «The mirror deflected the beam of light into the corner of the room.» Check the clues: the beam did not stop, it went in a new direction. Always try your meaning in the sentence: does "turned to a new direction" still make sense? It does, so you have it right.
fact: Deflect means to change direction, or to turn something away.
fact: In sport, a shot that hits a player and changes direction is a deflected shot.
fact: «Deflect the blame» means to pass the blame onto someone else.
fact: In science, mirrors deflect light and magnets deflect a compass needle.
exercise: «The shot hit the defender's leg and deflected into the net.» What does deflected mean here? | Became very soft | *Changed direction after hitting something | Was caught by the keeper | Went up into the sky forever
exercise: Mia tried to deflect the question by talking about her new bike. What did Mia do? | Cycled out of the classroom | Answered the question fully | Asked the question again, louder | *Turned the question away from herself
exercise: «The mirror deflected the beam of light.» What happened to the light? | It went out completely | It became much brighter | *It changed direction | It stayed exactly where it was
test: «The ball deflected off the wall and rolled back to Jamal.» What does deflected mean? | Stopped rolling completely | *Turned to a new direction after hitting something | Was thrown very hard by Jamal
test: The manager tried to deflect criticism onto the new worker. What did the manager try to do? | Accept all the criticism himself | Forget the criticism at once | *Pass the criticism to someone else
exam: «The magnet deflected the needle on the compass.» What does deflected mean in this science sentence? | Made the needle shine | Broke the needle | *Turned the needle to a new direction | Stuck the needle still
